The QA test file parameterizes 18 direct calls to `Window.handle_ClientMessage`, with cases for `_NET_WM_STATE`, `_NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW`, `_NET_CLOSE_WINDOW`, `WM_CHANGE_STATE`, `_NET_WM_DESKTOP`, and an unknown opcode. In `window.py`, those cases exercise the `_NET_WM_STATE` setup, loop, skip-zero path, add path, toggle path, and final property write; the `_NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW` pager path plus the non-pager focus, callable, scratchpad, smart-current-screen, smart-other-screen, urgent, never, and invalid-setting branches; the close branch; both `WM_CHANGE_STATE` assignments and the false auto-minimize check; the valid and invalid desktop reassignment paths; and the final unhandled-opcode debug path. Collecting the executed statements from those branches gives this sorted set of covered lines.

